Here's a full walk-through: create a concatenation transform, optionally chain an uppercase on top, verify the definition, then run it against a real identity through the profile preview endpoint — without touching the profile's live config.

---

## Step 1 — Create the concatenation transform

This builds `givenName.sn` from source account attributes.

```bash
TOKEN="<your-bearer-token>"
TENANT="<your-tenant>"

curl -s -X POST "https://${TENANT}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "demo-firstname-dot-lastname",
    "type": "concat",
    "attributes": {
      "values": [
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "attributeName": "givenName",
            "sourceName": "HR Source"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "static",
          "attributes": {
            "value": "."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "attributeName": "sn",
            "sourceName": "HR Source"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }'
```

Save the `id` (UUID) from the response — you'll need it for the preview call.

---

## Step 1b — Wrap it in uppercase (optional)

A second transform that references the first by **name** via the `reference` type:

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://${TENANT}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "demo-firstname-dot-lastname-upper",
    "type": "upper",
    "attributes": {
      "input": {
        "type": "reference",
        "attributes": {
          "id": "demo-firstname-dot-lastname"
        }
      }
    }
  }'
```

---

## Step 2 — Verify the stored definition

```bash
TRANSFORM_ID="<uuid-from-create-response>"

curl -s "https://${TENANT}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms/${TRANSFORM_ID}" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq .
```

Confirm `type`, `attributes.values`, and the `input` chain look correct before testing at runtime.

---

## Step 3 — Test output without touching the live profile

The identity profile preview endpoint accepts an `identityAttributeConfig` override, so you can inject your transform for one specific identity attribute and see the computed result — no profile edits required.

```bash
PROFILE_ID="<identity-profile-uuid>"
IDENTITY_ID="<test-identity-uuid>"

curl -s -X POST \
  "https://${TENANT}.api.identitynow.com/v3/identity-profiles/${PROFILE_ID}/preview" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "identityId": "'"${IDENTITY_ID}"'",
    "identityAttributeConfig": {
      "enabled": true,
      "attributeTransforms": [
        {
          "identityAttributeName": "uid",
          "transformDefinition": {
            "type": "reference",
            "attributes": {
              "id": "demo-firstname-dot-lastname"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }' | jq '.previewAttributes[] | select(.name == "uid")'
```

The response's `previewAttributes` array will show the current live value alongside the new computed value, letting you confirm the output before wiring the transform into the real profile mapping.

---

**Key points:**
- `reference.attributes.id` takes the transform's **name string**, not its UUID.
- The `upper` transform receives its input from the `input` attribute; the `concat` transform drives the input pipeline.
- You need a real identity whose source accounts are already correlated to see live data in the preview.

```answer-summary
